Subset types and newtypes now check that their constraints respect each declared covariant or contravariant type parameter, using the shared polarity analysis for member invariants. A conflicting occurrence is a resolution error. Previously a conversion between instantiations could skip a necessary constraint check and prove false. The existing check of the base type is unchanged. The hidden option `--legacy-unchecked-type-variance` restores the old, unsound rule for comparison and migration only.
